Z||000000||firstfiero||12-21-2001||02:32 PM||||   My wifes parents bought us a foosball table for christmas. It's a fun game for the family but unforunatly I really don't have room for it. My pool table takes up a large quanity of the basement. how much room do I need on either side of this thing? Anybody a foosball player out their?<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fleabitdog||12-21-2001||02:43 PM||||I would sell the pool table . Foosball is a great game the only thing is you can't play with yourself. Wait til you play enough that you get to the point where when you smack in a gaoal it sounds like it is going to bust out the back of the table.  Super!!! you can get by with about 3 ft on either side but I like to jump around. Good luck hope you can find someone to play with. Sucks looking at the table and not having an opponent.  Dave ||||reg||1
Z||000002||wkayl||12-21-2001||05:10 PM||||Spent many a quarters during noon hr at the Pondarosa Bar in Frederick SD during my high school years in the early 70's playing Foosball.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RiceCooker||12-21-2001||05:15 PM||||Yeah, 3 feet sounds like it's enough.<P>Have fun, they are definitely a blast. I blew a semester at University a couple years ago cause they had one in the arcade. I even had all the chinese guys askin me how i shot it so hard without spinning. <BR>My uncle used to be in a league so he's an allstar.<BR>Remember, no spinning and the centremen (is that what they're called) arent allowed to score.<P>Enjoy! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
